Then open browser to: http://localhost:5000

Option 3: Command Line Interface
For users who prefer terminal-based interaction.

bash
python scripts/tts_generator.py
🎮 Using the Interface
Gradio UI Guide
When you open the Gradio interface, you'll see:

Step-by-Step Usage:

Select a Voice - Click on any speaker name in the left panel

Enter Text - Type what you want the voice to say

Example: "Hello, this is a test of voice cloning"

Generate - Click the "Generate Speech" button

Wait - 2-5 seconds while the AI creates the audio

Listen - Audio automatically plays

Download - Click the download button to save the WAV file

Example Texts to Try:

"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"

"Welcome to my voice cloning demonstration"

"This sounds just like me! The quality is amazing"

CLI Mode Commands
If using the command line interface:

Command	What it does
list	Shows all available voices
switch	Changes to a different voice
save	Saves with a custom filename
quit	Exits the program

