🔧 Troubleshooting
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: "No module named TTS"
Solution: Install TTS specifically:

bash
pip uninstall TTS -y
pip install TTS==0.22.0
Issue 2: "CUDA out of memory"
Solution: Close other GPU applications and reduce text length, or edit config/settings.json:

json
{
    "model": {
        "gpu_memory_fraction": 0.7,
        "mixed_precision": true
    }
}
Issue 3: Model download stuck/fails
Solution: Manual download:

Go to https://huggingface.co/coqui/XTTS-v2

Download all files

Create folder models/xtts-v2/

Place downloaded files there

Issue 4: "Transformers" import error
Solution: Install correct version:

bash
pip uninstall transformers -y
pip install transformers==4.36.2
Issue 5: No voices registered
Solution: Run registration:

bash
python scripts/register_voices.py
Issue 6: Audio too long error
Solution: Trim your audio to 15-30 seconds using any audio editor (Audacity is free).

Issue 7: Poor voice quality / doesn't sound like me
Solution:

Use cleaner audio (no background noise)

Ensure 15-30 seconds of clear speech

Try different portions of your recording

Issue 8: IDM popups when downloading
Solution: Add 127.0.0.1 and localhost to IDM's exclusion list:

Open IDM → Downloads → Options

Go to "Site Management" tab

Add 127.0.0.1 and localhost

Select "Disable IDM for this site"

❓ Frequently Asked Questions
Q1: How many voices can I add?
A: Unlimited! Just create new folders in the voices directory and register them.

Q2: What's the best audio length?
A: 15-30 seconds gives the best results. Longer isn't necessarily better.

Q3: Can I use MP3 files?
A: Yes, but WAV is recommended for best quality. The system will convert MP3 to WAV automatically.

Q4: Does it work without an internet connection?
A: Yes, after the initial model download (1.8 GB), you can use it completely offline.

Q5: How long does generation take?
A: 2-5 seconds per sentence on a GPU, 10-20 seconds on CPU.

Q6: Can I use this for commercial purposes?
A: The XTTS-v2 model is for non-commercial use only. Contact Coqui.ai for commercial licensing.

Q7: Why is the first generation slow?
A: The model loads into memory on first use. Subsequent generations are faster.

Q8: Can I add more than 4 speakers?
A: Absolutely! The 4-speaker setup is just an example. Add as many as you want.

Q9: What languages are supported?
A: English is default, but XTTS-v2 supports multiple languages including Spanish, French, German, and more.
